description.en-US:
This module encapsulates the core deployment logic of the PolarDB-X Log Engine, automatically enabling and configuring a highly available, scalable log service component by associating with an existing instance ID. Its key features include:  
- Enabling the Log Engine service (`enable_log_engine = true`);  
- Specifying the CDC compute node class (`cdc_node_class`) and node count (`cdc_node_count`) to accommodate varying throughput requirements;  
- Supporting Multi-Streams mode to enhance parallel data subscription and distribution capabilities—ideal for complex real-time data warehousing, heterogeneous synchronization, and multi-consumer architectures;  
- Deep integration with the underlying PolarDB-X instance, eliminating the need to manually provision standalone resources and ensuring consistency in permissions, networking, and lifecycle management.  
This configuration serves as a critical infrastructure layer for building real-time data pipelines—such as Flink CDC ingestion, message queue synchronization, and lakehouse-integrated ETL.
